  :adr/context
  "CLAUDE.md fixes the runtime order as `kotoba wasm` > `clojurewasm` > ClojureScript >
nbb, with JVM and babashka demoted to last resort, and
`90-docs/migration/kotoba-wasm-runtime-cutover.edn` freezes a JVM inventory with
`:new-jvm-runtime-dependencies :forbidden` and `:new-chicory-call-sites :forbidden`.

That inventory has exactly FOUR entries, all under `orgs/kotoba-lang/`: kototama's
Chicory tender, aiueos' Chicory execute, kotoba's Chicory launcher, and the compiler
(now `amu`) Clojure bootstrap. `scripts/verify-kotoba-wasm-runtime-cutover.cljs` checks
those four deps.edn files and has been green throughout. Correctly green -- it is
answering the question it was asked.

Nobody had asked the other question. There are 4,183 west-registered repositories, and
until this measurement nothing looked at 4,179 of them. A rule the contract calls
FORBIDDEN was therefore unenforceable everywhere except in the four repositories that
already had it written down, and its enforcement gate could not have gone red no matter
what landed anywhere else."

  :adr/decision
  "1. **Measure the whole surface, and classify by what the JVM is FOR.**
     `scripts/verify-jvm-dependency-surface.cljs` (nbb, ~10s over 4,163 checkouts)
     replaces the four-file check's blind spot. It is registered in
     `manifest/orgs-detectors.edn` as `:verify-jvm-dependency-surface` (24h,
     `:writes :none`) rather than as a fleet gate, for the reason that file's header
     already gives: a gate ships only the target repo's tree and would find an empty
     workspace.

  2. **`.clj` sources and third-party jars are the debt. Test runners, linters and a
     bare `org.clojure/clojure` line are not.** The detector emits per-repo findings
     only for the former, and counts the latter. Lumping them reports a catastrophe and
     points at a rename.

  3. **A `:jvm-test` fleet gate may become `:nbb-test` only on three measurements, never
     on 'the sources are .cljc'.** Identical `Ran N tests containing M assertions` under
     both runtimes; the nbb entry exits non-zero with the subject broken and zero with it
     intact, failing for the thing that was broken; and no cross-repo dep on the test
     path, since `:nbb-test`'s classpath cannot reach a sibling. Recorded in
     `scripts/fleet-ci/gates.edn` at the head of `:repos`."

  :adr/body
  "## What was measured (2026-08-17, 4,163 of 4,183 registered checkouts on disk)

| class | repos | what the JVM is doing | emitted per repo |
|---|---|---|---|
| `:jvm-source` | 954 | `.clj` sources — the JVM is the runtime, not a tool | yes (fail) |
| `:jvm-runtime-deps` | 149 | a third-party JVM library in top-level `:deps` | yes (fail) |
| `:jvm-build` | 291 | shadow-cljs / cljs compiler / tools.build | yes (warn) |
| `:babashka` | 363 | `bb.edn`, retired by ADR-2607173000 | yes (warn) |
| `:jvm-chicory` | 3 | Chicory — **all three inside the frozen inventory** | yes (info) |
| `:jvm-runtime-clojure-only` | 1,292 | `org.clojure/clojure` alone in `:deps` | counted |
| `:jvm-test-oracle` | 1,656 | `.clj` tests (contract allows) | counted |
| `:jvm-test` | 3,278 | cognitect test-runner / kaocha in an alias | counted |
| `:jvm-lint` | 3,023 | clj-kondo via maven | counted |

Source totals: 2,752 `.clj` src, 6,436 `.clj` test, 25,385 `.cljc`, 2,829 `.cljs`,
2,037 `.kotoba`.

**The one class the contract calls forbidden has zero breaches.** All three Chicory
call sites are the frozen ones. That is a real green and it was unmeasured before now.

## Three ways the naive count is wrong, each measured

**Maven coordinates are not the question.** 3,683 of 3,994 `deps.edn` carry a
`:mvn/version`, which reads as near-total capture. 3,293 of those are a `clj-kondo`
lint alias — a tool with a native binary and an npm package.

**Reading `:deps`/`:extra-deps` is not enough.** clj-kondo's own recommended alias uses
`:replace-deps`. The first version of the detector found 30 clj-kondo sites where there
are 3,023.

**A git coordinate into this workspace is a graph edge, not a leaf.** 424 repos pin
`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph` with `:git/tag`+`:git/sha` and no `:git/url`; deriving
the org from the coordinate symbol the way the Clojure CLI does moved
`:jvm-runtime-deps` from 1,971 to 1,441.

**Unregistered checkouts must not be counted.** `orgs/` holds 4,581 repo-shaped
directories against west.yml's 4,183; the surplus is agent worktrees
(`.tamaki-tamaki-loop-*`, `.cloud-itonami-app-adopt`, `.wt-run`) contributing 3,281
`.clj` files — 15% of the raw total, every one a copy of a file already counted under its
registered path. Counting them makes the number move whenever a loop happens to run.

## The failure mode in 'just run it under ClojureScript'

56 fleet gates were `:jvm-test`. `nodes.edn` puts cap `:jvm` on 2 of 10 hosts (4 slots)
against `:node` on 4 (8 slots), and `placement.cljs` costs them 600s vs 180s — so moving
a gate off the JVM buys real queue time. 15 of the 56 target repos contain **zero `.clj`
files**, which looks like a green light.

It is not. On `columnar`, `test/run.cljs` and `test/columnar/cljs_runner.cljs` each
required ONE of the suite's three test namespaces:

```
JVM  (clojure -M:test)         Ran 36 tests containing 117 assertions
nbb  (test/run.cljs)           Ran 10 tests containing  54 assertions
```

Nothing prints the number it should have reached. With `group/group` altered to drop the
last group from every grouped result — a defect the JVM suite catches at once:

```
partial runner, broken source   Ran 10 tests, 0 failures, exit 0    <-- green
full runner,    broken source   Ran 36 tests, 2 failures, exit 1
full runner,    clean source    Ran 36 tests, 0 failures, exit 0    == JVM
```

Flipping that gate on the strength of `.clj == 0` would have moved it to a cheaper node
AND silently dropped two thirds of the suite, and the signed receipt would have looked
identical. This is ADR-2608136000's class — *the check that could not measure returns the
same value as the check that measured and found nothing* — reached from the direction of
a migration rather than a bug.

Fixed upstream first (`kotoba-lang/columnar` 5e165f0, both halves now 36/117), then
flipped.

## What was resolved, and what was refused

Flipped `:jvm-test` -> `:nbb-test` (56 -> 53 jvm-test, 1 -> 4 nbb-test), all three
measured on the three admission conditions:

| repo | tests / assertions, JVM == nbb | broken -> exit |
|---|---|---|
| `kagami` | 19 / 121 | 1 (west.yml trailing-line parse) |
| `columnar` | 36 / 117 | 1 (group dropped) |
| `org-ietf-csv` | 10 / 38 | 1 (quote char) |

Refused, with the reason recorded in `gates.edn` so it is not re-derived:

- **`kotobase-storage`** — its `test/run.cljs` is a COMPLEMENT, not a port. Its own
  docstring says the JVM half races real threads and covers the synchronous store, while
  this half covers the async/Worker path the JVM cannot reach. It prints no `Ran N tests`
  line at all, so the gate's own floor (exit 93) would reject it. Both halves are real
  coverage; dropping either loses tests.
- **`io-multiformats`, `org-ietf-cbor`** — their cljs half is `shadow-cljs compile`,
  itself a JVM build. No nbb entry exists.
- **`chain`, `io-ipld`, `io-ipld-car`, `nekko`, `org-apache-avro`, `kotobase-lake`,
  `tech-ipfs-specs-ipns`, `sakkyokuka`** — zero `.clj`, but the test path needs sibling
  repos through `deps.edn`, and `:nbb-test`'s classpath is the shipped tree only. The
  pre-existing note at `ongaku` in gates.edn records the same constraint.

## What is NOT claimed

The 954 `.clj`-source repositories and the 149 third-party-jar repositories are not
resolved. Each is a per-repo port (`.clj` -> `.cljc`, or a decision core to `.kotoba` per
ADR-2608650000's split between a permanent safety constraint and a backend that has not
caught up), and the third-party ones need a real cljs/npm substitute — `cheshire`,
`http-kit`, `ring-core`, `datalevin`, `transit-clj` have no cljs form, so the code that
requires them cannot run anywhere else today. The detector now names all of them
individually and reports a NEW one the next tick, which is the enforcement the four-entry
inventory could not provide.

`org.clojure/clojure` was NOT stripped from the 1,210 repos that declare it while
shipping zero `.clj`. It is a declaration, not a binding: nbb does not read `deps.edn` at
all, so removing the line changes nothing a consumer can observe, and a 1,210-repo sweep
whose effect is unobservable is the paperwork this ADR is arguing against."

  :adr/consequences
  "- `manifest/orgs-detectors.edn` gains an 11th detector; its first run recorded a
  baseline of 1,760 findings and the second reported none as NEW, verified against an
  isolated `--state`.
- The forbidden classes in `kotoba-wasm-runtime-cutover.edn` are now enforceable outside
  the four repositories that inventory names. That contract is unchanged and stays
  correct; its `:cutover/legacy-inventory` remains 4 entries, because those four are the
  Chicory/bootstrap debt specifically and not the workspace's whole JVM surface.
- Three fleet gates left the 4-slot `:jvm` bottleneck for the 8-slot `:node` pool, and
  `columnar`'s ClojureScript coverage went from 10/36 tests to 36/36 on both halves.
- The detector refuses rather than guesses: a west.yml with no `path:` entries, or paths
  with no checkouts, prints `SCANNED 0` and exits **2** — neither 0 nor 1 — so the tick
  records `:inconclusive`, never clean. Both directions measured.
- Anyone converting another `:jvm-test` gate must satisfy the three admission conditions
  at the head of `gates.edn` `:repos`. `.clj == 0` is explicitly not sufficient, and the
  columnar measurement is there as the reason."

